2. Decreased Blood Velocity: As the resistance to blood flow increases, the velocity of blood flow decreases. This is because the blood must flow more slowly to overcome the increased resistance.

3. Increased Blood Pressure: The increased resistance to blood flow also leads to an increase in blood pressure. As the blood must overcome the resistance, the pressure inside the blood vessels must increase to maintain the flow of blood.

