   \[
   0.044\% = 0.044 \times \frac{1}{100} = 0.00044
   \]

2. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride:**  
   \[
   \text{Mass of sodium fluoride} = \text{Concentration} \times \text{Volume} = 0.00044 \, \text{g/mL} \times 10 \, \text{mL} = 0.0044 \, \text{g}
   \]

3. **Convert grams to milligrams:**  
   \[
   0.0044 \, \text{g} = 0.0044 \times 1000 \, \text{mg} = 4.4 \, \text{mg}
   \]

Thus, the correct answer is \(\boxed{4.4 \, \text{mg}}\).
