2 CO (g) + O2 (g) → 2 CO2 (g)

We can use the standard molar entropies (S°) for each substance to calculate the change in entropy. The standard molar entropies for CO, O2, and CO2 are 188.7 J/mol·K, 205.0 J/mol·K, and 213.6 J/mol·K, respectively.

ΔS = ΣnS°(products) - ΣnS°(reactants)

