2. Process optimization: Optimize the operating conditions of the production process, such as temperature, pressure, and reactant flow rates, to maximize the yield and efficiency of the process. This can be achieved through the use of advanced process control systems and real-time monitoring of the process.

3. Energy efficiency: Implement energy-efficient technologies and technologies to reduce energy consumption during the production process. This can include using heat exchangers, waste heat recovery systems, and energy-efficient equipment.

4. Waste minimization: Minimize the generation of waste products and byproducts during the production process. This can be achieved by optimizing the process, using catalysts to increase selectivity, and recycling waste materials.

