   - Let x be the change in concentration of Fe(CN)$_6^{4-}$ formed.
   - Since 1 mole of Fe$^{3+}$ reacts with 6 moles of CN$^-$ to form 1 mole of Fe(CN)$_6^{4-}$, the change in concentration will be:
     - [Fe$^{3+}$] = 1.0 - x
     - [CN$^-$] = 0.25 - 6x
     - [Fe(CN)$_6^{4-}$] = x

