","The molecular formula C4H10O can exhibit two types of isomerism: chain isomerism and functional isomerism.

1. Chain isomerism: This type of isomerism occurs when the carbon atoms are arranged in different ways in the main chain of the molecule. For C4H10O, the possible chain isomers are:

   a. Butan-1-ol (CH3CH2CH2CH2OH)
   b. Butan-2-ol (CH3CH(OH)CH2CH3)

2. Functional isomerism: This type of isomerism occurs when the molecules have the same molecular formula but different functional groups. For C4H10O, the possible functional isomers are:

   a. Butan-1-ol (CH3CH2CH2CH2OH)
   b. Butan-2-ol (CH3CH(OH)CH2CH3)
   c. Butan-3-ol (CH3CH2CH(OH)CH3)
   d. Butan-1-ol (CH3CH2CH2CH2OH)
   e. Butan-2-ol (CH3CH(OH)CH2CH3)
