3. **The 90% of the list price is equal to the cost price plus 25% of the cost price.**
4. **Express this as an equation:**  
   \[ 0.9 \times \text{limit price} = x + 0.25x \]
   \[ 0.9 \times \text{limit price} = 1.25x \]
5. **Given that the left-hand side of the equation is 65.97, we have:**  
   \[ 0.9 \times \text{limit price} = 65.97 \]
   \[ \text{limit price} = \frac{65.97}{0.9} = 73.3 \text{ (approximately)} \]
