   \[
   f(x) = \begin{cases}
   1, \quad \text{if } x \in C, \\
   0, \quad \text{if} x \notin C.
   \end{cases}
   \]  
   This function is bounded and continuous.  

3. **Compute \( \int f \, d\mu_n \) and \( \int f \, d\mu \)**  
   - For each \( n \), \( \int f \, d\mu_n = \mu_n(C) \) because \( f \) is constant on \( C \).  
   - \( \int f \, d\mu = \mu(C) \) because \( f \) is constant on \( C \).  

4. **Apply the given condition (i)**  
