   45 \, \text{km/hr} \times \frac{1000 \, \text{m}}{1 \, \text{km}} \times \frac{1 \, \text{hr}}{3600 \, \text{s}} = 12 \, \text{m/s}
   \]

2. **Calculate the relative speed of the train relative to the jogger**:  
   \[
   12 \, \text{m/s} - 9 \, \text{m/s} = 3 \, \text{m/s}
   \]

3. **Determine the total distance the train covers to pass the jogger**:  
   The relative speed of the train is 3 m/s, and it takes 25 seconds to pass the jogger.  
   \[
   \text{Distance} = \text{Relative speed} \times \text{Time} = 3 \, \text{m/s} \times 25 \, \text{s} = 75 \, \text{m}
   \]

