To pave a rectangular courtyard 50 m long and 16 1/2 m wide, 165 paving stones, each measuring 2 1/2 m * a certain width, are required. What is the width of each paving stone?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","1. **Calculate the area of the rectangle:**  
   \[
   \text{Area} = \text{length} \times \text{width} = 50 \text{ m} \times 16.5 \text{ m} = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]

2. **Calculate the area of one paving stone:**  
   \[
   \text{Area of one paving stone} = 2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{width} = 2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{width}
   \]

3. **Set up the equation to find the width of the paving stone:**  
   \[
   165 \times (2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{width}) = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]

4. **Solve for the width:**  
   \[
   165 \times 2.5 \times \text{width} = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]
   \[
   412.5 \times \text{width} = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]
   \[
   \text{width} = \frac{825 \text{ m}^2}{412.5} = 2 \text{ m}
   \]

   Therefore, the width of each paving stone is \(\boxed{2 \text{ m}}\).
