   \text{Time in years} \times \text{Daily amount} = \text{Total amount}
   \]
   \[
   5 \times 150 = 750
   \]

2. **Calculate the total amount to be passed in the new time time:**
   \[
   750 + 6000 = 6750
   \]

3. **Calculate the number of years for the new repayment plan:**
   \[
   \text{Total amount} / \text{Daily amount} = \text{Time in years}
   \]
   \[
   6750 / 150 = 45
   \]

4. **Subtract the original time time to find the difference:**
   \[
   45 - 5 = 40
   \]

   The new repayment plan is \(\boxed{40}\) years.

