- \( \frac{1}{\lambda^5} \): The intensity is inversely proportional to the fifth power of wavelength, meaning that shorter wavelengths (higher frequencies) have higher intensities.
- \( e^{h c / \lambda k T} \): This term is the Boltzmann factor, which accounts for the exponential decrease in intensity at higher wavelengths due to the finite energy levels of the system.

