\[ \text{N}_2\text{O}_4 \rightleftharpoons 2\text{NO}_2. \]
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
1. **Calculate the molar mass of N₂O₄:**  
   \[
   \text{Molar mass of N}_2\text{O}_4 = 2 \times 14 + 4 \times 16 = 92 \text{ g/mol}
   \]

2. **Calculate the molecular weight of the gas mixture:**  
   \[
   \text{Molecular weight} = \text{Vapour density} \times 4 = 25.67 \times 4 = 102.68 \text{ g/mol}
   \]

3. **Let \( x \) be the fraction of N₂O₄ that dissociates.**  
   \[
   \text{Fraction of N}_2\text{O}_4 = 1 - x, \quad \text{Fraction of NO}_2 = 2x
   \]

4. **Calculate the average molecular weight of the gas mixture:**  
   \[
   \text{Average molecular weight} = (1 - x) \times 92 + 2x \times 46 = 102.68
   \]
   \[
   92 - 92x + 92x = 102.68 \implies 0 = 102.68 - 92 \implies x = 0.115
   \]

5. **Calculate the percentage of NO₂ molecules:**  
   \[
   \text{Percentage of NO}_2 = 2x \times 100 = 2 \times 0.115 \times 100 = 23\%
   \]

**Final Answer:**  
The percentage of NO₂ molecules in the gas at 100°C and 760 mm Hg is \(\boxed{23\%}\).

